			<div class="content" id="post-content-4857147">
									

<p>This is definitely a weird concept. The problem here is that you're going to have to define a magic system, at least the extreme basics of it, and then how these spells gained sentience and took on human form. Making it harder is that you've apparently decided to base it on the Catholic system, which is mostly defensive (thaumaturgy is more of a defensive art than anything else), rather than a more dynamic pagan system (which would actually be more likely for the sybiraks given when they were exiled to Syberia).</p>
<p>It doesn't help that spells in the SCP-U are based more on defense, such as protection and keeping SCP down.</p>
<p>Basically, you have what amounts to a new race that you're trying to describe, and so you need to have a pretty good hook. Figure out why people should care for it, why it matters, and go from there.</p>

