			<div class="content" id="post-content-4857104">
									

<p>The problem is that this is a classic &quot;thing that does a thing&quot; but that's about it. It's sort of cool in that it evolves as he ages, but then you do nothing with it.</p>
<p>Something to consider is that his life could be linked to the creatures on his head; you could predict how old he would be when he dies by comparing which age the creatures are in and extrapolating (or about early 30s).</p>
<p>Also, a number of scientists would be interesting in studying the creatures in order to get an idea of how evolution works; they could perform experiments to see how they would affect the creatures' evolution.</p>
<p>The bottom line is that there no real hook; there's no real reason to care about this as you described. That needs to be worked on. Otherwise, it's just an interesting idea.</p>

