						<a href="/forum/t-13932277/cognation">Cognation</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4857101">
									

<p>This isn't a cliché idea, really; there's just too much going on. You have multiple ideas (The Foundation finds blood and starts using it! The blood flows towards people thinking of certain things! Scranton Reality Anchors! 3001! Ichabod project! Dr. Scranton! Old gods! 231!), but they don't fit together thematically or mechanically. Trying to put all of them together leads to a complex mess that's less than the sum of its parts.</p>
<p>If one of the ideas presented here was excised and fleshed out it might make for a compelling article (the Foundation stumbling on anomalous blood and trying to meddle with it is probably the most compelling, though it would take some work to make it interesting), but as-is I'm not particularly enthused.</p>
<p>Good luck!</p>

